Cilium v1.20.2 (chart v1.20.2), Gateway API CRDs v1.6.2
Generated 2026-10-14 from versions.lock.yaml.

Pin rationale:
- v1.20.2 is the immutable Cilium release selected by versions.lock.yaml.
  It includes the v1.20 backport of Cilium PR #47737, moving the FnSetRetval
  feature probe into BPF and avoiding the agent-start failure observed with
  Cilium 1.19.6 on Linux 7.2. It supports the feature set committed under
  cilium/:
    - CiliumGatewayClassConfig (needs >= 1.17, gateways/cilium/gateway-class-config.yaml)
    - CiliumL2AnnouncementPolicy (>= 1.16, cilium/l2-policy.yaml)
    - CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool (>= 1.16, cilium/lb-pool.yaml)
    - Gateway API (>= 1.14)

Render method (helm template, not committed binaries):
  helm template cilium cilium/cilium --version 1.20.2 \
    --namespace kube-system --include-crds \
    --set l2announcements.enabled=true \
    --set externalIPs.enabled=true \
    --set kubeProxyReplacement=true \
    --set ipam.mode=kubernetes \
    --set routingMode=native \
    --set ipv4NativeRoutingCIDR=10.244.0.0/16 \
    --set autoDirectNodeRoutes=true \
    --set endpointRoutes.enabled=true \
    --set operator.replicas=1 \
    --set gatewayAPI.enabled=true \
    --set hubble.enabled=false
  The values mirror the previous Ansible install
  (ansible/roles/cilium/tasks/main.yml:49-62). In 1.20.2 the chart no
  longer has a top-level externalIPs value (that --set was a no-op against
  1.16.x charts); external-IP handling now comes from l2announcements +
  lbipam, both enabled in the render.

Deviations from the raw chart render:
- hubble.enabled=false: k8labs does not use Hubble (no relay/UI, research
  does not touch it). Disabling it drops the two helm-rendered Secret
  objects (cilium-ca, hubble-server-certs) that contain freshly generated
  private keys — keeping the committed manifests free of secrets per
  the pinned-manifest constraints.
- cilium.io CRDs are committed separately in 00-crds/ (22 Cilium CRDs), extracted
  verbatim from the pinned v1.20.2 source tree
  (pkg/k8s/apis/cilium.io/client/crds/{v2,v2alpha1}/), i.e. the exact CRD
  set the cilium-operator would otherwise register at startup
  (--skip-crd-creation=false). They are applied before the install manifests
  so CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool / CiliumL2AnnouncementPolicy /
  CiliumGatewayClassConfig and the rest exist even while the operator is
  not yet running (the config-init ClusterIP bootstrap blocks its start).
- Gateway API v1.6.2 standard resources are committed as one-document files
  named `00-gateway-api-*.yaml`, split to keep each CAPI Secret data value
  under the Kubernetes object-size budget. The v1.6.2 standard bundle's
  GRPCRoute CRD is omitted because the retained v1.6.2 experimental
  `00-crds/gateway.networking.k8s.io_grpcroutes.yaml` provides the same
  resource with its experimental schema; exactly one GRPCRoute CRD is
  installed. The standard bundle also includes BackendTLSPolicy, ListenerSet,
  TCP/TLS/UDP routes, and safe-upgrades admission policy resources. Cilium
  1.20.2 is built against sigs.k8s.io/gateway-api v1.6.2; the operator only
  DISCOVERS Gateway API CRDs and disables Gateway API when they are missing
  (operator/pkg/gateway-api/cell.go), so they must be applied separately.

